.TH RRUBOCOP 1 "September 2026" "rrubocop 0.7.7" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rrubocop \- 10x faster RuboCop drop-in
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rrubocop
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPATH\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
rrubocop is a 10x faster RuboCop drop-in. Same CLI, configs, and output
format, without maintaining RuboCop gems. It parses with tree-sitter
and does not require a Ruby runtime for linting or simple ERB.
Unsupported ERB still needs
.B ruby
(or
.B bundle exec ruby
). It reads
.B .rubocop.yml
and emits RuboCop-compatible diagnostics.
Parity targets rubocop 1.84.2 with rubocop-rails 2.34.3,
rubocop-performance 1.26.1, rubocop-rspec 3.9.0,
rubocop-rspec_rails 2.32.0, and rubocop-factory_bot 2.28.0
(see
.BR \-\-version ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR
Path to configuration file.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format: progress, text, json, github, quiet, files, emacs, simple.
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-autocorrect\fR
Apply safe autocorrections.
.TP
\fB\-A\fR, \fB\-\-autocorrect\-all\fR
Apply all autocorrections.
.TP
\fB\-\-only\fR \fICOPS\fR
Run only these cops (comma-separated).
.TP
\fB\-\-except\fR \fICOPS\fR
Exclude these cops.
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-list\-target\-files\fR
List files that would be linted.
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-cops\fR
List registered cop names.
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-cache\fR \fIFLAG\fR
Use result caching (\fItrue\fR) or don't (\fIfalse\fR). Default: \fItrue\fR.
Cache lives under $RRUBOCOP_CACHE_DIR or ~/.cache/rrubocop.
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-level\fR \fISEVERITY\fR
Minimum severity for exit code 1 (default: convention).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.BR 0
clean,
.BR 1
offenses,
.BR 2
error.
.SH SEE ALSO
rubocop(1)
